m in crisis, can make correct decisions quickly. Concerns: difficulty communicating ideas, egocentric, not willing to further education. No explicit technical competence, but decision-making and attention may imply competence. Crew cooperation is strong. Stress resilience strong. Reliability strong. Decision quality strong. Attention strong. Communication concerns but maybe manageable.\n\nCandidate B: strengths: very conscientious (reliability), handles stress very well, good at assessing weather, excellent computer skills, leadership potential. Concerns: can be grumpy, wrong tone, weak memory for numbers, pretentious. No crew cooperation data, no decision-making under time pressure data. So missing key criteria.\n\nGiven that we now have concrete evidence for C covering crew cooperation, stress, decision-making, while B lacks those, C seems stronger overall despite communication concerns. The panel's goal is to choose best overall fit, not overvalue one strength. C's strengths cover many critical criteria. Communication issues are important but maybe less than missing data. So I think we should shift recommendation to Candidate C.\n\nThus Agent 2 will now state that after reviewing new evidence, I now recommend Candidate C. Provide reasoning: C's stress resilience, decision-making, crew cooperation, reliability, attention, outweigh B's strengths and C's communication concerns.\n\nWe must reference prior discussion: mention Agent 3's points, and that we now have evidence for C's stress and decision-making, and that B still lacks crew cooperation data. Provide explicit facts: \"keeps calm in a crisis\", \"can make correct decisions quickly\", \"creates a positive atmosphere with his crew\", \"100% reliable\", \"excellent attention skills\". Also mention concerns: \"difficulty communicating ideas\", \"egocentric\", \"not very willing to further his education\". Conclude that overall C is best.\n\nThus produce PUBLIC_MESSAGE and METADATA_JSON with vote Candidate C."}
